# --- atompipe project state ---
# A project carries its own ignore rules: `init` (and the one-time migration)
# writes a marked block into `<project>/.atompipe/.gitignore` — the generated
# index `ledger.json`, `cache/`, `obs/`, `out/` — and one into the project's root
# `.gitignore` for bytecode. The records (`claims/` and the rest) and the verdict
# cache `.atompipe/verdicts/` stay TRACKED. What slipped through: this comment
# still said `.atompipe/ledger.json` and `.atompipe/runs/` stay tracked after
# Phase 1 made the ledger an index nothing reads for truth and removed the run
# history — the migration rewrote every project's ignore file and nothing checked
# the repository's own.
# (METHOD.md rule 1: generated files are outputs, not sources.) Below: the scratch
# a hand-run check script writes beside a pack.
.atompipe/out/
.selftest-out/

